THE ENCOUNTER TABLE HOLE (s60) -- a (zone, topograph, fog) triple with NO record means NO encounter.

Stock's w_worldGetBattleScenePtr returned the zone slice's LAST record on a lookup miss
(ff9.cs:9209, `return w_frameBattleScenePtr[i + useAlternate - 1]` with i == zoneInfoEnd), which
made an authored table hole IMPOSSIBLE: any area's unlisted terrain rolled its zone's final row.
Found in-game (R4b, 2026-07-26): kit ground stamped area 14 (zone 6, records only at topos 10/36)
still fought zone 6's last record on topo-0 grass. The fix returns null on the miss; SelectScene
treats null as scene 0 (= no battle, the same contract ProcessEncount already honors).

Stock blast radius, censused before authoring: EXACTLY ONE spot map-wide exercises the fallthrough
-- 22 stray area-10 topo-0 tiles in blocks (20,14)/(21,14)/(22,14) (open-plains slivers inside the
zone-4 mountain region), which in stock fight zone 4's topo-36 brush row (rec 43) there. Under s60
those 22 tiles become encounter-silent -- arguably fixing a stock authoring quirk. Every other
walkable stock (zone, topograph, fog) triple has a real record (full census in
studies/overworld-topography/southern-ring/REVERT.md s27).

This is the engine half of THE TABLE IS THE LAW: the kit authors safety by stamping open ground
into a table-hole area (area 14, the SAFE-ROAD stamp, REVERT.md s26); s60 makes the hole real.

